        <headline>Flood Watch issued September 26 at 12:10PM PDT until September 29 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS Las Vegas NV</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.

* WHERE...A portion of northwest Arizona, including the following
areas, Hualapai Mountains, Northwest Deserts and Northwest Plateau.

* WHEN...From early Monday morning through Tuesday evening.

* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,
creeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.
Low-water crossings may be flooded.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- Showers and thunderstorms capable of producing flash flooding.
- Kingman, Colorado City, Valentine, Dolan Springs, Wikieup, Peach
Springs.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood
Warnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared
to take action should flooding develop.</instruction>
